course: dictionary
lesson: 4816
title: Words that name a place and its people
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you where something comes from. «Hungarian» is one of them. It means from or connected with Hungary, a country in central Europe. In «the Hungarian composer Zoltan Kodaly», Hungarian tells you where the composer came from.
explain: The same word can name a person or a language, and the sentence tells you which. A Hungarian is a person from Hungary. Hungarian is also the language spoken there. In «speak Hungarian», the word means the language.
explain: Check the meaning by swapping in a phrase. «The Hungarian composer» can become «the composer from Hungary», and the sentence still makes sense. That tells you Hungarian is describing the composer, so it is working as a describing word.
fact: Hungarian means from or connected with Hungary, a country in central Europe.
fact: A Hungarian is a person from Hungary.
fact: Hungarian is also the language spoken in Hungary, and it is called Magyar there.
fact: Hungarian is not a Slavic or Germanic language. It belongs to the Uralic family and is distantly related to Finnish.
fact: «Austro-Hungarian» means connected with Austria-Hungary, a country that existed in the past.
exercise: «In the Kodaly method, named after the Hungarian composer Zoltan Kodaly, "ta" is said for a one-beat note.» What does Hungarian mean here? | A type of drum | Very old | *From or connected with Hungary | A song about the sea
exercise: Anna says, «I speak Hungarian at home.» What does Hungarian mean here? | A tasty stew | *The language spoken in Hungary | A person from Hungary | A country in Europe
exercise: «Ukrainians fought in both the Russian and the Austro-Hungarian armies.» Find and copy the word that means connected with Austria and Hungary. | Ukrainians | armies | *Austro-Hungarian | opposite
test:  Maria is a Hungarian who lives in Budapest. What is a Hungarian? | A city in Hungary | *A person from Hungary | A type of stew | A river in Europe
test:  Hungary has its own language, also called Magyar. What is it called in English? | *Hungarian | Hungary | Hungarians | Austro-Hungarian
exam:  Hungarian is not a Slavic or Germanic language. Which family does it belong to? | Germanic | *Uralic | Romance | Slavic
